# KEDA was evaluated for autoscaling live-calculator and removed again: each KEDA
# pod costs a full 250m CPU minimum on Autopilot regardless of actual usage, and its
# redis-queue-depth trigger can only react after a task is already queued - it can't
# pre-warm ahead of a known contest start. Both jobs are now done by a scheduler
# thread inside tracker-processor (src/calculator_pool_scaler.py), which reads
# Contestant.tracker_start_time directly and scales the live-calculator Deployment
# via the Kubernetes API - no separate autoscaler component, no idle cost. If KEDA
# is ever reintroduced, uninstall first:
#   helm uninstall keda -n keda && kubectl delete namespace keda
